      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Please. I have been struggling with this for years since they provided these shaders. I have a great deal of avatars that I cant upload to quest because the models have vertex color data that I can't remove because I don't use Blender. So often the head or body will become black with green or blue bits here and there with no way to fix them. \n\nI use Maya which, importing content made by other programs, often causes the normals data on the models to break. Normally I can fix the issue if it's a model I made, because I built it in Maya, so there are no issues with breaking normals.\n\nI don't understand why the Lightmapped shader is blacklisted for avatars, but it's the only shader they provided us for quest that doesn't use the vertex color data.\n\nThe ability to use a Quest shader that disables the vertex color data would save me so much time and effort, along with not having to awkwardly ask other people to help me.\n\nThis for both Standard and Toonlit shaders.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-03T03:08:09.144Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Having settings to enable and disable vertex coloring (and maybe even enabling it for emissions) in the VRC mobile shader would be a cool option to have since most models don't use vertex shading.",
